 - The show of each line must match exactly what that line says.
 - Line 1 is an excited hook that names the topic (e.g. "Hi friends! Let's count stars with Boo!").
 - Last line ends the story happily and loops back to the start (e.g. "Yay! Pip found it! Let's play again!").
-- For good habits (brushing teeth, washing hands, sharing, please and thank you, tidying up, kindness, fruit, sleep, sorry, taking turns) use show type "text" with a fitting prop (heart, star, sun, moon, flower, apple) and a 1-2 word label like "SHARE!" or "BRUSH!".
+- For good habits use show type "text" with ONLY the prop named in the habit (toothbrush, apple, moon, star, car, balloon, square, heart) and a 1-2 word label that matches that picture (e.g. toothbrush + "BRUSH!", apple + "YUMMY!", moon + "SLEEP!", heart + "SORRY!"). Never show an unrelated object (no sun for washing, no apple for soap).
 - For a nursery rhyme only use the traditional public-domain words of that rhyme (first verse, shortened), plus a short hook and ending line.
 - Every line has a "show" object describing a big simple picture: type is one of color, count, letter, shape, text.
